### Lab 5: Key-value structure — string, JSON, list
### String value
curl -i -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/demo_values/keys/greeting \
  -H 'Content-Type: text/plain' \
  -d 'Hello from Riak KV'
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/demo_values/keys/greeting

### JSON document value
curl -i -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/demo_values/keys/student-json \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"id":"S002","name":"Diya Verma","course":"BCA"}'
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/demo_values/keys/student-json

### List value encoded as JSON
curl -i -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/demo_values/keys/interests \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '["analytics","databases","design"]'
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/demo_values/keys/interests

### Explanation:
### Bucket = logical namespace/collection; key = unique identifier inside bucket;
### value = opaque stored bytes (the application interprets it as text/JSON/list).
